{#
  partials/ioc-download-controls.njk — export the current search results
  ==========================================================================
  Included inside a `.ioc-search` panel (immediately after the filter chips,
  before the results count) on /remote-workers/, a cluster page and
  /repo-scanner/. Lives inside that panel on purpose: the panel itself starts
  `hidden` and is revealed only once ioc-search.js has loaded the index, so a
  reader without JavaScript never sees a control that could not work for them
  — the static whole-index and per-type CSV/JSON links in the page's
  <noscript> block are the export path for that reader instead. On
  /remote-workers/ this is the only download control a reader with
  JavaScript sees.

  ioc-search.js reads [data-ioc-download-format] and wires
  [data-ioc-download-button] to build a file client-side from whatever the
  current search text and filters have narrowed the result list to (`matches`
  in that script), not the full dataset. The only choice here is the format:
  the type filter above already narrows by type, so a second type control here
  only duplicated it.
#}
<div class="filter-chips" data-ioc-download>
  <span class="filter-chips__label">Download these results</span>
  <select data-ioc-download-format aria-label="Download format" data-short-label="Format">
    <option value="stix">STIX 2.1 bundle (JSON)</option>
    <option value="misp">MISP event (JSON)</option>
    <option value="csv">CSV</option>
    <option value="txt">Plain text (values only)</option>
    <option value="json">JSON</option>
  </select>
  <button type="button" class="btn btn--secondary" data-ioc-download-button>Download</button>
</div>
<p class="form-hint" data-ioc-download-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
